88:    88	- Code checks cited IDs against records: evidence must belong to this thesis and not be replaced; cited theses must be its dependencies. Accept only if all checks pass. Otherwise record the reason and ask for one corrected judgement. If that also fails, use normal failure handling: retry from this step, then human review after repeated failure. This checks references, not whether the judgement is correct, like verifying a cited page exists.
104:   104	- Count independent original sources. Twenty outlets retelling one exclusive are twenty references to one evidence item, not twenty independent confirmations.
106:   106	- Store evidence once without an intrinsic direction. Each rejudgement writes its push on the evidence–thesis link. One statement can affect multiple theses differently.
113:   113	B depends on A | What kind of thesis is A? (For an asset thesis B, state which end of A is bullish for B. For a theme thesis B, state whether their ladders have the same or opposite orientation.)
