docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-2-interrupted.txt:11:5. **H1’s proposed shortcut is broader than its cited rule.** [Plan line 90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:90) leans toward merging because the same annual-report note checks both amounts. A single document can report two independently moving amounts. The standard requires the *same result* to settle both and also requires scope to distinguish financing from guarantees ([standard, lines 293–294 and 316–319](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:293)). D210’s one-deal-or-programme wording does not establish that sharing a note makes two questions identical ([D210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2670)).
docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-2-interrupted.txt:13:6. **H2 describes a later question without yet showing how it survives until then.** [Plan lines 91 and 171](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:91) merge a later deadline into an earlier question, then propose opening a successor after expiry. The earlier question keeps its fixed deadline and outcomes ([PRD 06, lines 74–75](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:74)); the present succession path acts when matching a candidate ([code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:284)). The plan leaves the later deadline’s preservation and the event that creates the successor to a future table. Without those, Kyber’s 2028 question can be lost if no new article arrives after 2027.
docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-2-interrupted.txt:19:I re-ran the corrected census read-only: **122 candidates, 39 merges and 2 successions** for the sealed ledger, and **32 candidates, 12 merges and 1 succession** for v38. The reported evidence counts match the census outputs, subject to the plan’s correct qualification that “same claim” labels are estimates. H3 now names the conflicting milestone rule; H4 is presented as a choice; and H7’s lean preserves D204. I did not independently verify every cost estimate, every archived verdict classification, or every factual claim in the plan.
