docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-6.txt:11:The central source checks support several corrections already made. The guarantee/financing sentence is in both the [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318) and the [collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1); its causing the ACP split remains unproven, as the plan now says. H1–H7 identify their principal changes as choices, and H7’s lean agrees with [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2609). The displayed census totals match the saved outputs, but verdict classes still depend on reason-text parsing ([census script line 25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:25)). I did not independently verify every archived verdict, quote, estimate, or factual claim.
docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-2.txt:13:6. **H4’s lean does not name the period conflict it creates.** [Plan line 94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:94) proposes folding a calendar-year question into a fiscal-year question because company quantities use fiscal years. But the example differs in both period and scope, and the [standard lines 274 and 316–317](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:274) distinguish one period, the same result, and a later period. The fiscal-year writing rule does not itself establish that these are the same result. H3 names its conflicting separation rule; H4 should likewise present this as an unresolved change to the identity boundary.
docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-2.txt:19:I re-ran the corrected census read-only: its outcome totals match the plan—sealed **69 questions, 122 candidates, 39 merges, two successions**; v38 **17, 32, 12 and one**. The verdict-category counts remain provisional because the [script parses reason text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:18), as the plan acknowledges. The signed standard and prompt do both contain the guarantee/financing example. H7’s revised lean preserves D204’s two records, and H3 now names the relevant separation rule and D236. Cost estimates and every individual census classification were not independently verified.
