docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-3.txt:9:4. **H1’s lean adds an unacknowledged exception to the signed rule.** [Plan line 92](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:92) says different transactions should be separate when counterparties or assets differ. The [signed standard line 319](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:319) instead says a transaction judged to be part of an already-open amount-based programme merges into it. The lean names D210 and the two standard sentences, but does not identify this specific conflict. Whether the examples are actually part of one programme still needs source-based judgment.
