docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-1.txt:17:7. **H2 and H5 do not fully cover the existing identity contract.** H2’s proposed merge keeps the earlier question’s fixed outcomes and due date; the plan does not show how a later deadline remains answerable after the earlier deadline passes. The existing question and outcomes are immutable ([PRD 06 lines 8 and 14](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:8)); succession is continued tracking after an event question closes ([line 176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:176)). H5 says code would retain only object, type and due year ([plan line 90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:90)); that omits scope, event type and other distinctions currently used by [identity.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:18). It could coalesce separate events, and the plan does not enumerate that risk.
