docs/DECISIONS.md:2599:- Regression week ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), `english-v34b-nvda-week-2026-10-27`, $0.23, 98 items, none failed): the whole path runs with the revision rule; `replacements` gains no row. Counts differ from the v18 week (129 against 176 evidence rows, 12 against 9 theses) because extraction is a sampler, not because of the writer; the writer's effect is proved on the decisions themselves. Reading the week's one `replace` decision found a second silent loss in the same code path: an incoming statement said before its target was logged in `late_statements` and linked nowhere (both weeks dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report this way; the three-month run dropped the SharonAI backstop figure; 1 of 3,216 decisions, each a material statement). Fixed in the same slice: an older statement is stored and linked as one more piece, no revision recorded, the log row kept. Test red on the old writer, green after; suite 209. Observed, not fixed here: 34 of 1,530 stored pieces carry a non-ISO `original_day` ("2026-07-05 to 2026-07-06", "2026-03"), which is what made the Kyber report "older"; an extraction-contract item for the next pass.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2730:- A new [reference candidate](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/gold-user-2026-10-29-v2/reference.json) preserves the complete old gold and week candidate as immutable base data, and records only the answer overlays. The revenue-growth expectation is core; the specific FY2028 EPS is excluded; SK hynix's shortage forecast and hyperscaler spending estimates are core; the AMD 100 kW modeled comparison and Omniverse change are colour. Sharon is supply/demand support; NVL72x2 concerns product progress; neither answer asserts a specific page or adds a rule that different products are identical. The Google Cloud revenue, growth and backlog form one gold item, with all three parts needed to claim complete meaning.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2782:- D222 result: 19 of 48 planned comparison calls returned complete responses (10 control, 9 treatment); one treatment fabricated a question ID and was refused, so the remaining 29 were not sent. Target facts stayed present (7/7 control, 6/6 treatment observations), but both treatment NVIDIA answers turned unknown signing status into unsigned in admission reasoning and one called Firmus an unnamed builder. Both arms also asserted a shared WSJ origin for old reports without sufficient provenance. The prompt is not adopted; there is no stable-improvement claim from these incomplete repeats. All calls, readings and unissued slots are preserved in the linked results. No additional paid arm, production code, default, gold or ledger change.

