  2703	- Alex requested actual traces, useful retention and correct junk removal, with one overall acceptance basis rather than further piecemeal fixes. The [audit](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/results.md) uses the same 98 stored items in v36b/v37/v38 at $0. It changes no product rule or default.
  2704	- All 841 v38 extraction records were labelled M (material), C (context/marginal) or J (clear junk); 127 written M records were read beside their quotes and destinations. Earlier configurations have 1,522 records, of which 1,316 inherit the same article's exact/contained quote label and 206 were read separately. Labels are Codex-authored, not independent human gold. Actual written evidence is 106/54/144, versus the old intermediate handover counts 108/55/146.
  2705	- Material written: 67/47/127; precision among written records: 63.2%/87.0%/88.2%; retention among already-extracted material: 23.0%/17.4%/44.9%. V38 correctly removes 254/255 clear junk records and 541/558 nonessential records including C. Of its 697 lost records, 156 are M. Three written M records are under the wrong product's question.
  2706	- A fixed, source-first-for-this-pass 20-article reference contains 33 material claims, 25 core. Five articles had been inspected earlier and are explicitly not an unseen holdout. Complete final claims: 12/5/13; complete core claims: 12/4/11. V38 improves on v37 but does not establish better core completeness than v36b. Each version has one stored run; these differences do not measure sampling stability.
  2707	- Trace census of v38's 156 material losses: 94 have no corresponding question all week; 49 have the destination shown; 7 belong to an unshown candidate of their own item; 4 precede a later question; 1 fails the quote check and 1 disappears after matching rejects its candidate. The earlier claim that matching alone owns the remaining loss, or duplicate pages explain the placement misses, is withdrawn.
  2708	- D190 remains a bounded next comparison, not a validated remedy for these losses. Its ACP pairs are directly affected; revenue/growth bypasses its same-measure gate and launch/shipment also conflicts at the identity check. A link-relabeling diagnostic reduces 17 pages to 13 and 178 links to 152 while retaining the same 144 records, restoring none of the drops; this is not a new model result. Any later improvement claim must report final core retention, meaning, placement and junk alongside page count, using the fixed reference. No paid call or production edit in this audit.
